From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:22:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] dt-bindings: input: apple,dockchannel-hid: document the
 kiwi interface properties

The kiwi (touch screen) interface of the dockchannel MTP owns its power
sequencing lines instead of sharing the multi-touch analog front end
reset. Document apple,power-method, apple,reset-gpios and
apple,power-gpios on the kiwi child node, mirroring how the multi-touch
child documents its power method. Without apple,reset-gpios the driver
falls back to the shared AFE reset of the parent and does not power-cycle
the touchscreen itself; the text says so.

The 24 MHz clock and display sync pads are pad functions selected by the
transport node pinctrl, not GPIO properties, so they need no binding
entries.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit b1e78d5fcc993ca3d9688e408282c13f44fef768)
---
 .../bindings/input/apple,dockchannel-hid.yaml | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/apple,dockchannel-hid.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/apple,dockchannel-hid.yaml
index 598ab3da81..20984450f1 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/apple,dockchannel-hid.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/apple,dockchannel-hid.yaml
@@ -231,6 +231,33 @@ properties:
           Name of the touchscreen firmware that the host sends to the
           coprocessor when the interface is first opened.
 
+      apple,power-method:
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+        enum: [1, 2]
+        default: 1
+        description:
+          The power sequencing protocol of the coprocessor firmware, as
+          described above. With power method 2 the touchscreen owns its
+          lines, so apple,reset-gpios should be given. Without it the driver
+          falls back to the shared apple,afe-reset-gpios of the parent and
+          does not power-cycle the touchscreen itself.
+
+      apple,reset-gpios:
+        maxItems: 1
+        description:
+          Reset line of the touchscreen, described with the level that
+          asserts the reset as its active level. Unlike the multi-touch
+          analog front end reset the touchscreen owns the line, and with
+          power method 2 the host drives it itself during the start
+          sequence instead of using the shared reset of the parent.
+
+      apple,power-gpios:
+        maxItems: 1
+        description:
+          Optional supply enable line of the touchscreen, raised to power
+          the interface on and lowered to power it off during power
+          method 2 transitions.
+
   mtp:
     type: object
     additionalProperties: false
